From: GlassGlide contributors
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: compile Document.cpp outside unified bundles

Document.cpp is particularly large. Combining it with seven other sources
exhausts the shared build host's memory when cross-compiling with GCC.
Compile it separately so the build remains incremental and uses less memory.

--- a/Source/WebCore/Sources.txt
+++ b/Source/WebCore/Sources.txt
@@ -1302,7 +1302,7 @@ dom/DeviceOrientationAndMotionAccessController.cpp
 dom/DeviceOrientationController.cpp
 dom/DeviceOrientationData.cpp
 dom/DeviceOrientationEvent.cpp
-dom/Document.cpp @header:RenderStyleGetters @cost:22
+dom/Document.cpp @header:RenderStyleGetters @cost:22 @no-unify
 dom/DocumentFontLoader.cpp
 dom/DocumentFragment.cpp
 dom/DocumentFullscreen.cpp
